  "note": "Triennial election of the Ballymena Urban Council, January 1929. Market Ward was uncontested after Mr. William Cameron's withdrawal; Town Hall and Harryville Ward were contested. Six nominations were lodged but Mr. William Cameron withdrew, leaving five for five seats. Returned unopposed.",
